"children":"Home organization"}],["$","h1",null,{"children":"No-drill window treatments: the renter's guide to blackout, privacy, and warmth"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"article-dek","children":"How to cover a rental window with zero hardware—pick the right no-drill mount, choose blackout vs light-filtering, and make budget curtains look expensive."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"article-meta","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":["8 min"," read"]}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Updated ","August 2026"]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Research-based guide"}]]}]]}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"article-visual","children":[["$","$Le",null,{"src":"/pins/renter-window-treatments-no-drill.png","alt":"No-drill renter window guide graphic: pick your no-drill mount, blackout vs light-filtering, cellular shades for insulation and privacy, and cheap curtains that look pricey.","width":1000,"height":1500,"priority":true}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":"Saveable Beep Bot Picks checklist — the full advice stays below."}]]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"takeaway","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Beep’s bottom line"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"You can black out, insulate, and dress any rental window without a single hole—but only if you match the treatment to a no-drill mount that actually holds, and measure before you buy so you don't return it."}]]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"shopping-box","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Useful shopping shortcuts"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"affiliate-disclosure","children":"This guide contains affiliate links. As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases, and we may earn from qualifying eBay purchases."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"shopping-links","children":["$Lf","$L10","$L11","$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15"]}],"$L16"]}],"$L17","$L18","$L19"]}]
