17:["$","div",null,{"className":"article-body","children":[["$","section","Pick your no-drill mount first",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Pick your no-drill mount first"}],[["$","p","The treatment matters less than what holds it up. In a rental you have three ways to cover a window without a drill, and each one fails in a different way if you skip the fine print.",{"children":"The treatment matters less than what holds it up. In a rental you have three ways to cover a window without a drill, and each one fails in a different way if you skip the fine print."}],["$","p","Decide the mount before you fall for a shade, because a gorgeous panel on the wrong mount just sags, gaps, or peels the paint on the way out.",{"children":"Decide the mount before you fall for a shade, because a gorgeous panel on the wrong mount just sags, gaps, or peels the paint on the way out."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Tension rod: springs inside the window frame, holds curtains or a cafe panel. Buy one rated well past your inside width and with a fatter diameter so it won't bow and drop.",{"children":"Tension rod: springs inside the window frame, holds curtains or a cafe panel. Buy one rated well past your inside width and with a fatter diameter so it won't bow and drop."}],["$","li","Adhesive brackets: stick above the frame for roller and cellular shades. They hold only if the surface is smooth, clean, and given the full cure time before you load them.",{"children":"Adhesive brackets: stick above the frame for roller and cellular shades. They hold only if the surface is smooth, clean, and given the full cure time before you load them."}],["$","li","Over-the-frame / magnetic: hooks that hang over a wood frame, or magnets on a steel door, add curtains with nothing permanent at all.",{"children":"Over-the-frame / magnetic: hooks that hang over a wood frame, or magnets on a steel door, add curtains with nothing permanent at all."}]]}]]}],["$","section","Blackout vs light-filtering: choose by room",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Blackout vs light-filtering: choose by room"}],[["$","p","\"Blackout\" and \"room-darkening\" are not the same claim, and buying the wrong one is the most common window return.",{"children":"\"Blackout\" and \"room-darkening\" are not the same claim, and buying the wrong one is the most common window return."}],["$","p","Match the level to what the room is actually for, and remember that side gaps—not the panel itself—are what let dawn in.",{"children":"Match the level to what the room is actually for, and remember that side gaps—not the panel itself—are what let dawn in."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Bedroom or nursery: true blackout, mounted to overlap the frame on all four sides so light doesn't leak at the edges.",{"children":"Bedroom or nursery: true blackout, mounted to overlap the frame on all four sides so light doesn't leak at the edges."}],["$","li","Living or dining room: light-filtering keeps privacy and a soft glow without making the room a cave.",{"children":"Living or dining room: light-filtering keeps privacy and a soft glow without making the room a cave."}],["$","li","West- or east-facing glass: add thermal blackout to cut the afternoon heat and morning glare, not just the light.",{"children":"West- or east-facing glass: add thermal blackout to cut the afternoon heat and morning glare, not just the light."}],["$","li","Measure the window's width and drop before ordering any shade—sized-to-fit is the whole point.",{"children":"Measure the window's width and drop before ordering any shade—sized-to-fit is the whole point."}]]}]]}],"$L1a","$L1b","$L1c"]}]
18:["$","div",null,{"className":"article-note","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Editorial note"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"This guide contains no paid placement. Clearly labeled affiliate links may earn us a commission and do not change what you pay."}]]}]
19:["$","section",null,{"className":"related-guides","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"section-kicker","children":"Keep reading"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"Related practical guides"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","$L2","small-space-entryway-organization",{"href":"/guides/small-space-entryway-organization/","children":["A small entryway needs landing zones, not more storage bins"," ",["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":"→"}]]}],["$","$L2","dorm-move-in-no-drill-checklist",{"href":"/guides/dorm-move-in-no-drill-checklist/","children":["The no-drill dorm move-in checklist that protects your deposit"," ",["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":"→"}]]}],["$","$L2","budget-usb-c-hub-buying-guide",{"href":"/guides/budget-usb-c-hub-buying-guide/","children":["The USB-C hub checklist that prevents a bad buy"," ",["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":"→"}]]}]]}]]}]
1a:["$","section","Cellular shades: insulation and privacy in one",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Cellular shades: insulation and privacy in one"}],[["$","p","A cellular (honeycomb) shade is the renter's quiet overachiever: the pockets trap air, so it insulates against heat and cold while it darkens the room.",{"children":"A cellular (honeycomb) shade is the renter's quiet overachiever: the pockets trap air, so it insulates against heat and cold while it darkens the room."}],["$","p","It's also the easiest no-drill shade to get wrong on fit, so check these before you buy.",{"children":"It's also the easiest no-drill shade to get wrong on fit, so check these before you buy."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Cordless is child- and pet-safe and looks cleaner—skip the dangling pull.",{"children":"Cordless is child- and pet-safe and looks cleaner—skip the dangling pull."}],["$","li","Single cell is fine for privacy; double cell insulates more if the window is drafty.",{"children":"Single cell is fine for privacy; double cell insulates more if the window is drafty."}],["$","li","Confirm it mounts inside the frame with adhesive brackets, not screws.",{"children":"Confirm it mounts inside the frame with adhesive brackets, not screws."}],["$","li","Measure the exact inside width at top, middle, and bottom—old frames aren't square, and the narrowest number is the one that fits.",{"children":"Measure the exact inside width at top, middle, and bottom—old frames aren't square, and the narrowest number is the one that fits."}]]}]]}]
1b:["$","section","Make budget curtains look expensive",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Make budget curtains look expensive"}],[["$","p","Cheap curtains read cheap for three fixable reasons: they're too skimpy, hung too low, and made of flat fabric. Fix all three and a $30 panel passes for far more.",{"children":"Cheap curtains read cheap for three fixable reasons: they're too skimpy, hung too low, and made of flat fabric. Fix all three and a $30 panel passes for far more."}],["$","p","None of it requires drilling—just a well-chosen tension or over-frame rod and a little height.",{"children":"None of it requires drilling—just a well-chosen tension or over-frame rod and a little height."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Use panels totaling about double the window width so they gather full instead of stretching flat.",{"children":"Use panels totaling about double the window width so they gather full instead of stretching flat."}],["$","li","Hang the rod high and wide—near the ceiling and past the frame—so the window looks taller and bigger.",{"children":"Hang the rod high and wide—near the ceiling and past the frame—so the window looks taller and bigger."}],["$","li","Pick slub linen or a linen-cotton weave; the texture reads high-end and hides wrinkles between washes.",{"children":"Pick slub linen or a linen-cotton weave; the texture reads high-end and hides wrinkles between washes."}],["$","li","Let them just kiss the floor; puddling looks fussy and short looks like a mistake.",{"children":"Let them just kiss the floor; puddling looks fussy and short looks like a mistake."}]]}]]}]
1c:["$","section","Upgrade curtains you already own",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Upgrade curtains you already own"}],[["$","p","If you like your curtains but they let light through, don't rebuy—add a hookable blackout liner behind them.",{"children":"If you like your curtains but they let light through, don't rebuy—add a hookable blackout liner behind them."}],["$","p","It clips onto the same rings, blocks light, and adds a thermal layer, turning any panel into a blackout panel with no sewing and no new mount.",{"children":"It clips onto the same rings, blocks light, and adds a thermal layer, turning any panel into a blackout panel with no sewing and no new mount."}]],"$undefined"]}]
